cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PEN-COMPARE, please cite:"
type: software
title: "PEN-COMPARE: Hierarchical Certification Framework for Non-Destructive Genome Editors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-05-26"
authors:
  - family-names: Mahaboob Ali
    given-names: Anees Ahmed
    affiliation: "VIT University, Vellore"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmedanees-m/pen-compare"
url: "https://ahmedanees-m.github.io/pen-compare"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  PEN-COMPARE (Programmable Editor Nominee - Comparative Outcome Metrics via
  Pre-registration and Axis-based Ranking Evaluation) is the capstone of the
  PEN-STACK framework. It applies a 5-gate hierarchical
  TrueWriterScore certification system to a unified universe of 1,058 genome
  editors and computational designs (29 natural IS110-family editors + 1,029
  pen-assemble designs), integrating four upstream packages: GENOME-ATLAS,
  MECH-CLASS, PEN-SCORE, and PEN-ASSEMBLE. The framework certifies editors
  as TRUE_WRITER, PROBABLE_WRITER, EMERGING_WRITER, or NOT_WRITER. All four
  pre-registered predictions (P1-P4) passed validation. ISCro4 is confirmed
  as the sole TRUE_WRITER with robustness = 1.000 across 20,480 parameter
  combinations. A local-LLM RAG Q&A system (88%
  benchmark accuracy) deliver the results interactively.
keywords:
  - genome-engineering
  - bridge-recombinase
  - IS110
  - writer-not-scissors
  - PEN-STACK
  - bioinformatics
  - certification-framework
  - true-writer
  - molecular-pen
  - RAG-LLM
  - pre-registration
